(7485192, 1190848, 172697, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations on your HM!  <br/> <br/>This is a fabulous image... I love it that you''ve caught a "shooting star".<br/> <br/>Oddly, though... I''d have cropped the image just below that... to really make it about that dreamy place between heaven and earth that you''ve captured.<br/> <br/>I think it gets a bit lost with all of the stuff up top making it all about the stuff up top.  :D </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for your feedback Lydia!<br/> <br/>The fact here is that I actually wanted this picture to be "almost" all about the stuff up top!<br/> <br/>The title "Down to Earth" refers to the shooting star, so I''ve never would have cropped it out :)<br/> <br/>I''m glad you enjoyed this picture, thanks again for stopping by!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Lydia: Congratulations on your HM!   This is a fabulous image... I love it that you''ve caught a "shooting star". Oddly, though... I''d have cropped the image just below that... to really make it about that dreamy place between heaven and earth that you''ve captured. I think it gets a bit lost with all of the stuff up top making it all about the stuff up top.  :D   Thank you for your feedback Lydia! The fact here is that I actually wanted this picture to be "almost" all about the stuff up top! The title "Down to Earth" refers to the shooting star, so I''ve never would have cropped it out :) I''m glad you enjoyed this picture, thanks again for stopping by! ', '2016-11-30 13:59:51.000000', NULL, 0),
